  "reason": "The best result so far is config_029 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250), with config_008 (same but concat) close behind at 0.7207. The evidence strongly favors scvi_n200 over scgpt and multimodal over RNA-only. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler avgpool aggregation could match or exceed it when paired with the best fusion (weighted) and best encoders (scvi_n200 + vit_l). Config_042 isolates this single variable (aggregation: transformer→avgpool) while holding all other components at their empirically best settings. This is a minimal, high-information experiment: if avgpool performs comparably, it confirms the architecture is robust; if it underperforms, it confirms transformer aggregation is a critical component. With 4 experiments remaining after this, establishing whether aggregation matters is essential before committing to further refinements."
}

